diff --git a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Input.md b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Input.md
index 62f70b5a..19f7bc21 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Input.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Input.md
@@ -2,9 +2,10 @@
 
 In this section you can configure input devices like keyboard and mouse, and some input-related options.
 
-There's a section for each device type: `keyboard`, `touchpad`, `mouse`, `trackpoint`, `trackball`, `tablet`, `touch`.
-Settings in those sections will apply to every device of that type.
-Currently, there's no way to configure specific devices individually (but that is planned).
+Each device type has a section: `keyboard`, `touchpad`, `mouse`, `trackpoint`, `trackball`, `tablet`, or `touch`.
+An unnamed `keyboard` section configures all keyboards.
+A named `keyboard` section overrides the default settings for one keyboard.
+The other device sections apply to every device of their type.
 
 All settings at a glance:
 
@@ -130,6 +131,32 @@ input {
 }
 ```
 
+#### Per-device settings
+
+Add the libinput device name to a `keyboard` section to configure one keyboard.
+Name matching ignores ASCII letter case.
+Named settings merge over the unnamed keyboard settings.
+Later matching sections take precedence.
+
+```kdl
+input {
+    keyboard {
+        xkb {
+            layout "us"
+            variant "dvorak"
+        }
+    }
+
+    keyboard "ZMK Project SliceMK ErgoDox Keyboard" {
+        xkb {
+            layout "us"
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+Niri changes the active keymap when it receives an event from a different keyboard.
+
 > [!TIP]
 >
 > <sup>Since: 25.02</sup>
